  "goodToKnow": "Der Hochmut is arrogance or haughty pride, one of the seven deadly sins (die Todsünden). The proverb Hochmut kommt vor dem Fall (pride goes before a fall) comes from the Book of Proverbs. Hochmütig means haughty. Der Stolz can be positive pride, while Hochmut is always negative. Its opposite is die Demut (humility). It has no plural."
